{"title": "Sectional Mock #16 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>The least number which is exactly divisible by 3, 8, 5, 12, and 4. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2379; 3, 8, 5, 12 &#2324;&#2352; 4 &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2340;&#2307; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2379;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["120", "100", "90", "150"], "options_hi": ["120", "100", "90", "150"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>L.C.M of 3, 8, 5, 12, and 4 = 120</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>L.C.M of 3, 8, 5, 12, and 4 = 120</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a + b + c = 5, a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup> = 85 and abc = 25, then find the value of a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a + b + c = 5, a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup> = 85 &#2324;&#2352; abc = 25 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> - ab - bc - ca &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;:</p>", "options_en": ["2", "4", "6", "8"], "options_hi": ["2", "4", "6", "8"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><b>We know that:</b></p><p>a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup>  -  3abc = (a + b + c) (a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>85  -  3 * 25 = 5(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>17  -  3 * 5 = (a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>17  -  15 = (a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca = 2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>We know that:</b></p><p>a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup>  -  3abc = (a + b + c) (a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>85  -  3 * 25 = 5(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>17  -  3 * 5 = (a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>17  -  15 = (a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca = 2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Evaluate: &radic;(10 + 2&radic;21) &#8722; &radic;(10 &#8722; 2&radic;21)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;: &radic;(10 + 2&radic;21) &#8722; &radic;(10 &#8722; 2&radic;21)</p>", "options_en": ["2&radic;3", "&radic;21", "4", "&radic;7"], "options_hi": ["2&radic;3", "&radic;21", "4", "&radic;7"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>10 + 2&radic;21 = (&radic;7 + &radic;3)<sup>2</sup> &rarr; &radic;(10 + 2&radic;21) = &radic;7 + &radic;3</p><p>10 &#8722; 2&radic;21 = (&radic;7 &#8722; &radic;3)<sup>2</sup> &rarr; &radic;(10 &#8722; 2&radic;21) = &radic;7 &#8722; &radic;3</p><p>Difference = (&radic;7 + &radic;3) &#8722; (&radic;7 &#8722; &radic;3) = 2&radic;3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>10 + 2&radic;21 = (&radic;7 + &radic;3)<sup>2</sup> &rarr; &radic;(10 + 2&radic;21) = &radic;7 + &radic;3</p><p>10 &#8722; 2&radic;21 = (&radic;7 &#8722; &radic;3)<sup>2</sup> &rarr; &radic;(10 &#8722; 2&radic;21) = &radic;7 &#8722; &radic;3</p><p>Difference = (&radic;7 + &radic;3) &#8722; (&radic;7 &#8722; &radic;3) = 2&radic;3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p><b>Directions:</b>   The following graph shows the distribution (degree wise) of students who attended five different seminars.</p><p>The total number of students who attended all seminars = 5400</p><p><img width=289 height=278 id=\"Chart 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18239/image003.png\"></p><p>The percentage of students attended seminar A is: (up to one correct decimal)</p>", "q_hi": "<p><b>&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342;&#2375;&#2358;:</b> &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2354;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2352;&#2339; (&#2337;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;) &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p>&#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2354;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; = 5400</p><p><img width=\"289\" height=\"278\" id=\"Chart 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18239/image003.png\"></p><p>&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2354;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;: (&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2340;&#2325;)</p>", "options_en": ["33.8%", "29.6%", "33.6%", "29.8%"], "options_hi": ["33.8%", "29.6%", "33.6%", "29.8%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Given that,</p><p>360&deg; = 100%</p><p>1&deg; = (100/360) %</p><p>121&deg; = 100 * 121/360 = 33.6%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given that,</p><p>360&deg; = 100%</p><p>1&deg; = (100/360) %</p><p>121&deg; = 100 * 121/360 = 33.6%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Achinta, Bobby, Cindrella working together completed a job in 10 days. However, Cindrella only worked for the first three days when 0.37 part of the job was done. Also, the work done by Achinta in 5 days is equal to the work done by Bobby in four days. How many days would be required by the fastest worker to complete the entire work?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2330;&#2367;&#2344;&#2340;&#2366;, &#2348;&#2377;&#2348;&#2368;, &#2360;&#2367;&#2306;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; 10 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2361;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;, &#2360;&#2367;&#2306;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2348; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 0.37 &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404;&#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2361;&#2368; &#2309;&#2330;&#2367;&#2344;&#2340;&#2366; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 5 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2348;&#2377;&#2348;&#2368; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2375;&#2332;&#2364; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["20 days", "30 days", "25 days", "40 days"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "30 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "25 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "40 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The equations are:</p><p>3 (A + B + C) = 37% of the work.</p><p>7 (A + B) = 63% of the work.</p><p>So, A + B = 9% of the work --- (1)</p><p>Where A, B, C are one day's work of Achinta, Bobby and Cindrella respectively.</p><p>Further 5A = 4B --- (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2), A = 4% of the work and B = 5% of the work</p><p>In 3 days (A + B + C) do 37% of the work.</p><p>Out of that, A + B do 9% each day.</p><p>Hence, in three days, (A + B) X 3 = 27% of the work.</p><p>Remaining work in first three days = 37 - 27 = 10% of the work </p><p>So, Cindrella would do 3.33% of the work in a day.</p><p>Thus Bobby is the fastest and he would complete it in 20 days.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The equations are:</p><p>3 (A + B + C) = 37% of the work.</p><p>7 (A + B) = 63% of the work.</p><p>So, A + B = 9% of the work --- (1)</p><p>Where A, B, C are one day's work of Achinta, Bobby and Cindrella respectively.</p><p>Further 5A = 4B --- (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2), A = 4% of the work and B = 5% of the work</p><p>In 3 days (A + B + C) do 37% of the work.</p><p>Out of that, A + B do 9% each day.</p><p>Hence, in three days, (A + B) X 3 = 27% of the work.</p><p>Remaining work in first three days = 37 - 27 = 10% of the work </p><p>So, Cindrella would do 3.33% of the work in a day.</p><p>Thus Bobby is the fastest and he would complete it in 20 days.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p> A tank is connected with 8 pipes some are inlet pipes and rest are outlet pipes. Each of inlet pipe can fill the tank in 8 hours individually while each outlet pipe can empty the tank in 6 hours individually if all pipes are kept open when the tank is empty, it will take 8 hours for the tank to fill. How many of these are outlet pipes?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; 8 &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2369;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2311;&#2344;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2310;&#2313;&#2335;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2311;&#2344;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; 8 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2310;&#2313;&#2335;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2366; 6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2326;&#2369;&#2354;&#2375; &#2352;&#2326;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 8 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2310;&#2313;&#2335;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["5", "3", "6", "2"], "options_hi": ["5", "3", "6", "2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "\"<p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/4f4db9e5477db51815dc06fb683a8321.png\"> </p><p> Now, the tank is filled in 8 hrs</p><p> So, in 1 hr qty. filled=3</p><p> for 5 inlet pipe and 3 outlet pipe , </p><p> qty filled in 1 hour=5&#215;3-3&#215;4=3 units</p><p>so, clearly there are 5 inlet and 3 outlet pipes.</p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/4f4db9e5477db51815dc06fb683a8321.png\"> </p><p> Now, the tank is filled in 8 hrs</p><p> So, in 1 hr qty. filled=3</p><p> for 5 inlet pipe and 3 outlet pipe , </p><p> qty filled in 1 hour=5&#215;3-3&#215;4=3 units</p><p>so, clearly there are 5 inlet and 3 outlet pipes.</p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average of five consecutive odd numbers is 25. What is the largest of these numbers?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 25 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["27", "29", "31", "33"], "options_hi": ["27", "29", "31", "33"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Five consecutive odd numbers can be written as n - 4, n - 2, n, n+2, n+4; their average = n</p><p>So n = 25; largest = n + 4 = 29</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Five consecutive odd numbers can be written as n - 4, n - 2, n, n+2, n+4; their average = n</p><p>So n = 25; largest = n + 4 = 29</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>Riya sold an item to Vani at 10% loss and Vani sold it to Maya at Rs. 4950 at 10% profit. Riya bought the item by spending -</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2339;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 10% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2339;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2351;&#2361; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; 4950 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 10% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 7000", "Rs. 2000", "Rs. 5000", "Rs. 5300"], "options_hi": ["7000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "2000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "5000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "5300 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost price of item for Riya = m</p><p>Cost price of item for Riya = 0.9m</p><p>Cost price of item for Maya = 0.9m * 110/100 = 0.99m</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>0.99m = 4950</p><p>m = 4950/0.99</p><p>m = Rs. 5000</p><p><b>Alternate method-</b></p><p>Let the cost price of item for Riya = m</p><p>m * 0.9 * 1.1 = 4950</p><p>m = 4950/0.99 = Rs. 5000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost price of item for Riya = m</p><p>Cost price of item for Riya = 0.9m</p><p>Cost price of item for Maya = 0.9m * 110/100 = 0.99m</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>0.99m = 4950</p><p>m = 4950/0.99</p><p>m = Rs. 5000</p><p><b>Alternate method-</b></p><p>Let the cost price of item for Riya = m</p><p>m * 0.9 * 1.1 = 4950</p><p>m = 4950/0.99 = Rs. 5000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>In how many ways can a football team of 9 players be chosen from 14 players?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>14 &#2326;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 9 &#2326;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335;&#2348;&#2377;&#2354; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1890", "2002", "1996", "2140"], "options_hi": ["1890", "2002", "1996", "2140"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total number of ways = <sup>14</sup>C<sub>9</sub> = <sup>14</sup>C<sub>5</sub> = 14*13*12*11*10/(5*4*3*2*1) = 2002</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total number of ways = <sup>14</sup>C<sub>9</sub> = <sup>14</sup>C<sub>5</sub> = 14*13*12*11*10/(5*4*3*2*1) = 2002</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>For what value of k will be following system of equations have no solution? </p><p>(k  -  1)x + 9y + 3 = 0, 14x  -  6y + 17 = 0</p>", "q_hi": "<p>k &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2361;&#2354; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p>(k - 1)x + 9y + 3 = 0, 14x - 6y + 17 = 0</p>", "options_en": ["20", "18", "-20", "-18"], "options_hi": ["20", "18", "-20", "-18"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Rearranging the equation:</p><p>(k  -  1)x + 9y =  - 3</p><p>14x  -  6y =  - 17</p><p>For no solution:</p><p>a<sub>1</sub>/a<sub>2</sub> = b<sub>1</sub>/b<sub>2</sub> &#8800; c<sub>1</sub>/c<sub>2</sub> </p><p>(k  -  1)/14 = 9/(-6) &#8800; -3/-17</p><p>(k  -  1)/14 = 9/(-6)</p><p>k  -  1 = - 21</p><p>k = -20</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Rearranging the equation:</p><p>(k  -  1)x + 9y =  - 3</p><p>14x  -  6y =  - 17</p><p>For no solution:</p><p>a<sub>1</sub>/a<sub>2</sub> = b<sub>1</sub>/b<sub>2</sub> &#8800; c<sub>1</sub>/c<sub>2</sub> </p><p>(k  -  1)/14 = 9/(-6) &#8800; -3/-17</p><p>(k  -  1)/14 = 9/(-6)</p><p>k  -  1 = - 21</p><p>k = -20</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify the following expression</p><p>0.07  X  0.28 &div; 0.04 + 0.64 - 1.64 &div; 0.04</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2352;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;</p><p>0.07 X 0.28 &div; 0.04 + 0.64 - 1.64 &div; 0.04</p>", "options_en": ["38.56", "-39.87", "-46.48", "36.78"], "options_hi": ["38.56", "-39.87", "-46.48", "36.78"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>0)07  X  0.28 &div; 0.04 + 0.64 - 1.64 &div; 0.04</p><p>=&gt; 0.49 + 0.64  -  41 = -39.87</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>0)07  X  0.28 &div; 0.04 + 0.64 - 1.64 &div; 0.04</p><p>=&gt; 0.49 + 0.64  -  41 = -39.87</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>P can do a piece of work alone in 9 days, Q can do the same work alone in 18 days, while R can do it alone in 27 days. They work together and complete the work and receive a total of &#8377;726 as payment for doing the work. What is the combined share of Q and R, taken together from the above amount?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>P &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 9 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, Q &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 18 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; R &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2311;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 27 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#8377;726 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2313;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; Q &#2324;&#2352; R &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2369;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;270", "&#8377;300", "&#8377;330", "&#8377;360"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;270", "&#8377;300", "&#8377;330", "&#8377;360"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>We know, wages and time are inverse of each other.</p><p>Time ratio, P : Q : R = 9: 18: 27 = 1: 2: 3</p><p>Then, wages ratio, P : Q : R = (1/1): (1/2): (1/3) = 6: 3: 2</p><p>Total wages = &#8377;726</p><p>Therefore, share of Q and R together = 726 * (3 + 2)/(6 + 3 + 2) = &#8377;330</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know, wages and time are inverse of each other.</p><p>Time ratio, P : Q : R = 9: 18: 27 = 1: 2: 3</p><p>Then, wages ratio, P : Q : R = (1/1): (1/2): (1/3) = 6: 3: 2</p><p>Total wages = &#8377;726</p><p>Therefore, share of Q and R together = 726 * (3 + 2)/(6 + 3 + 2) = &#8377;330</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>If cosY = 8/17, then the value of sinY*secY*tanY is ________.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; cosY = 8/17, &#2340;&#2379; sinY*secY*tanY &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; ________ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["225/64", "15/8", "1", "225/136"], "options_hi": ["225/64", "15/8", "1", "225/136"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>cosY = 8/17</p><p>Base = 8, Hypotenuse = 17</p><p>Perpendicular = &radic;(17<sup>2</sup>  -  8<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= &radic;(25*9)</p><p>= 15</p><p>=&gt; sinY*secY*tanY</p><p>= 15/17 * 17/8 * 15/8</p><p>= 225/64</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>cosY = 8/17</p><p>Base = 8, Hypotenuse = 17</p><p>Perpendicular = &radic;(17<sup>2</sup>  -  8<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= &radic;(25*9)</p><p>= 15</p><p>=&gt; sinY*secY*tanY</p><p>= 15/17 * 17/8 * 15/8</p><p>= 225/64</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>A vertical pole of length 6 m casts a 4 m long shadow on the ground. At the same time, a tower casts a 28 m long shadow. Find the height of the tower. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>6 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2314;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2343;&#2352; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366; &#2332;&#2350;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; 4 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2368; &#2331;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352; 28 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2368; &#2331;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["42 m", "32 m", "36 m", "48 m"], "options_hi": ["42 &#2350;&#2368;", "32 &#2350;&#2368;", "36 &#2350;&#2368;", "48 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>As angle of elevation is same for both tower and pole,</p><p>So</p><p>Similar triangles: Pole height/shadow = Tower height/shadow </p><p>6 / 4 = h / 28 </p><p>h = 28  X  (6 / 4) = 7 &#1093; 6 = 42 m.</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>As angle of elevation is same for both tower and pole,</p><p>So</p><p>Similar triangles: Pole height/shadow = Tower height/shadow </p><p>6 / 4 = h / 28 </p><p>h = 28  X  (6 / 4) = 7 &#1093; 6 = 42 m.</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum becomes Rs.4525 in 5 years and Rs.5430 in 6 years when compounded annually at some rate of interest. What is the simple interest on Rs.6400 at the same rate of interest in 7.5 years?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 4525 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 6 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 5430 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 7.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; 6400 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.9000", "Rs.9600", "Rs.8400", "Rs.8000"], "options_hi": ["9000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "9600 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "8400 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "8000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>For compound interest:</p><p>Let the rate of interest = R% and sum = Rs. P</p><p>Then, amount in 5 years; </p><p>4525 = P X  (1+ R/100)<sup>5</sup></p><p>And, amount in 6 years; </p><p>5430 = P  X  (1+R/100)<sup>6</sup></p><p>Now, 4525/5430 = 1/(1+R/100) </p><p>R=20</p><p>Therefore, SI on Rs.6400 at 20% rate of interest in 7.5 years;</p><p>6400  X  20  X  7.5/100= = Rs. 9600</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>For compound interest:</p><p>Let the rate of interest = R% and sum = Rs. P</p><p>Then, amount in 5 years; </p><p>4525 = P X  (1+ R/100)<sup>5</sup></p><p>And, amount in 6 years; </p><p>5430 = P  X  (1+R/100)<sup>6</sup></p><p>Now, 4525/5430 = 1/(1+R/100) </p><p>R=20</p><p>Therefore, SI on Rs.6400 at 20% rate of interest in 7.5 years;</p><p>6400  X  20  X  7.5/100= = Rs. 9600</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>AB and AC are two tangents to the circle. BD is the diameter of the circle which is produced to meet C and E is the point on the circle where AC touches the circle. If EC = 35 cm and BD = 24 cm then find the length of AE.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>AB &#2324;&#2352; AC &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; BD &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; C &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; E &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2361; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; AC &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; EC = 35 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; BD = 24 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; AE &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["12.4 cm", "16.8 cm", "17.1 cm", "8.7 cm"], "options_hi": ["12.4 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "16.8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "17.1 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "8.7 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=243 height=202 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21879/image010.jpg\"></p><p>In &#8710;EOC-</p><p>OC<sup>2</sup> = OE<sup>2</sup> + EC<sup>2</sup></p><p>OC<sup>2</sup> = 12<sup>2</sup> + 35<sup>2</sup></p><p>OC = 37 cm</p><p>BC = 37 + 12 = 49</p><p>Let AB = AE = 'a' cm</p><p>In &#8710;ABC-</p><p>AC<sup>2</sup> = AB<sup>2</sup> + BC<sup>2</sup></p><p>(a + 35)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + 49<sup>2</sup></p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + 1225 + 70a = a<sup>2</sup> + 2401</p><p>a = 16.8 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=243 height=202 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21879/image010.jpg\"></p><p>In &#8710;EOC-</p><p>OC<sup>2</sup> = OE<sup>2</sup> + EC<sup>2</sup></p><p>OC<sup>2</sup> = 12<sup>2</sup> + 35<sup>2</sup></p><p>OC = 37 cm</p><p>BC = 37 + 12 = 49</p><p>Let AB = AE = 'a' cm</p><p>In &#8710;ABC-</p><p>AC<sup>2</sup> = AB<sup>2</sup> + BC<sup>2</sup></p><p>(a + 35)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + 49<sup>2</sup></p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + 1225 + 70a = a<sup>2</sup> + 2401</p><p>a = 16.8 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p> The speeds of two boats A and B in still water are 7.5 m/s and 12.5 m/s respectively and the speed of the stream is 2.5 m/s. If the time taken by boat A to go &#8216;x&#8217; m upstream and came back, is 16 seconds more than the time taken by boat B to go &#8216;x&#8217; m upstream and came back, then find the time taken by boat B to go &#8216;x&#8217; m upstream and came back. </p><p> </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357;&#2379;&#2306; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 7.5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2324;&#2352; 12.5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 2.5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 'x' &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2310;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351;, &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 'x' &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2310;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; B &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 'x' &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2310;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["16 seconds", "24 seconds", "20 seconds", "12 seconds"], "options_hi": ["16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "24 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "\"<p>The upstream speed of boat A = 7.5 &#8211; 2.5 = 5 m/s</p><p>The downstream speed of boat A = 7.5 + 2.5 = 10 m/s</p><p>The upstream speed of boat B = 12.5 &#8211; 2.5 = 10 m/s</p><p>The downstream speed of boat B = 12.5 + 2.5 = 15 m/s</p><p>According to the question:</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/866378092acdc56db3857cf3b8a0839c.png\" /> </p><p> The time taken by boat B to go 120 m upstream and came back = \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000078.png\"/>\r + \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000079.png\"/>\r = 20 seconds</p><p> </p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p>The upstream speed of boat A = 7.5 &#8211; 2.5 = 5 m/s</p><p>The downstream speed of boat A = 7.5 + 2.5 = 10 m/s</p><p>The upstream speed of boat B = 12.5 &#8211; 2.5 = 10 m/s</p><p>The downstream speed of boat B = 12.5 + 2.5 = 15 m/s</p><p>According to the question:</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/866378092acdc56db3857cf3b8a0839c.png\" /> </p><p> The time taken by boat B to go 120 m upstream and came back = \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000078.png\"/>\r + \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000079.png\"/>\r = 20 seconds</p><p> </p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three cards are drawn one after another with replacement from a pack of cards. What is the probability of getting the first card as an ace of black, the second as red, and the third as a number card that is divisible by 3?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2366;&#2358; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2337;&#2381;&#2337;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2352;&#2306;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2311;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366;, &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2354; &#2352;&#2306;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2311;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; 3 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1/2704", "1/1352", "3/1352", "3/2704"], "options_hi": ["1/2704", "1/1352", "3/1352", "3/2704"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Ace of black = 2, Red = 26, divisible by 3 = 3 [3, 6, 9] </p><p>Hence, the required probability = 2/52 * 26/52 * 3/52 </p><p>= 3/2704</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ace of black = 2, Red = 26, divisible by 3 = 3 [3, 6, 9] </p><p>Hence, the required probability = 2/52 * 26/52 * 3/52 </p><p>= 3/2704</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Probability"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the remainder if 43<sup>43</sup> + 43 is divided by 44.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 43<sup>43</sup> + 43 &#2325;&#2379; 44 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["0", "43", "42", "41"], "options_hi": ["0", "43", "42", "41"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=68 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22135/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=112 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22135/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=188 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22135/image009.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=68 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22135/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=112 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22135/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=188 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22135/image009.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 561: 11:: 510: x and y: 266 :: 42: 228, then find (2x + y).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 561: 11:: 510: x &#2324;&#2352; y: 266 :: 42: 228 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (2x + y) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p>", "options_en": ["54", "69", "72", "81"], "options_hi": ["54", "69", "72", "81"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Here, 561: 11:: 510: x</p><p>x = 510 * 11/561 = 10</p><p>And, y: 266 :: 42: 228</p><p>y = 266 * 42/228 = 49</p><p>Therefore, 2x + y = 2 * 10 + 49 = <b>69</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here, 561: 11:: 510: x</p><p>x = 510 * 11/561 = 10</p><p>And, y: 266 :: 42: 228</p><p>y = 266 * 42/228 = 49</p><p>Therefore, 2x + y = 2 * 10 + 49 = <b>69</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the total surface area (in sq. cm) of a cone if the base radius of cone is 7/2 cm and slant height of the cone is 4 cm.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 7/2 cm &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 4 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (sq. cm &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["82.5", "76.5", "88.4", "105.2"], "options_hi": ["82.5", "76.5", "88.4", "105.2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Total surface area = &#960; * r * (l + r)</p><p>= (22/7) * (7/2) * [4 + (7/2)]</p><p>= 11 * 15/2</p><p>= 82.5 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total surface area = &#960; * r * (l + r)</p><p>= (22/7) * (7/2) * [4 + (7/2)]</p><p>= 11 * 15/2</p><p>= 82.5 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pomegranate juice contains 10% sugar solution and orange juice contains 30% sugar solution. What is the percentage of sugar solution in a mixture of two litres of pomegranate juice and three litres of orange juice? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 10% &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 30% &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2309;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2360; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? </p>", "options_en": ["22%", "25%", "20%", "40%"], "options_hi": ["22%", "25%", "20%", "40%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Pomegranate: 2L  X  10% = 0.2L sugar </p><p>Orange: 3L  X  30% = 0.9L sugar </p><p>Total sugar = 0.2 + 0.9 = 1.1L </p><p>Total volume = 2 + 3 = 5L </p><p>Percentage = (1.1 / 5)  X  100 = 22% </p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Pomegranate: 2L  X  10% = 0.2L sugar </p><p>Orange: 3L  X  30% = 0.9L sugar </p><p>Total sugar = 0.2 + 0.9 = 1.1L </p><p>Total volume = 2 + 3 = 5L </p><p>Percentage = (1.1 / 5)  X  100 = 22% </p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>A vendor at a local fair claims to sell sugar at &#8377;72 per kg, which is also his actual cost price. However, to earn a hidden profit, he gives only 700 grams instead of 1 full kilogram. What is the vendor's actual profit percentage?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; 72 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2366;&#2357;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2349;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2361;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;, &#2331;&#2369;&#2346;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2357;&#2361; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; 700 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["37.85%", "40.85%", "39.85%", "42.85%"], "options_hi": ["37.85%", "40.85%", "39.85%", "42.85%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Gain = (Faulty weight  -  actual weight) * 100/actual weight</p><p>= (1000  -  700) * 100/700</p><p>= 42.85%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Gain = (Faulty weight  -  actual weight) * 100/actual weight</p><p>= (1000  -  700) * 100/700</p><p>= 42.85%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The sum and difference of LCM and HCF of two numbers are 146 and 38 respectively. If the sum of numbers is 154, then find the larger number.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; LCM &#2324;&#2352; HCF &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 146 &#2324;&#2352; 38 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 154 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["112", "42", "46", "108"], "options_hi": ["112", "42", "46", "108"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>LCM + HCF = 146 ....... (i)</p><p>LCM  -  HCF = 38 ....... (ii)</p><p>From (i) and (ii), we get -</p><p>LCM = 92</p><p>HCF = 54</p><p>Let, the numbers be x and (154  -  x).</p><p>x * (154  -  x) = 92 * 54</p><p>=> 154x  -  x<sup>2</sup> = 4968</p><p>=> x<sup>2</sup>  -  154x + 4968 = 0</p><p>=> x<sup>2</sup>  -  (46 + 108)x + 4968 = 0</p><p>=> x = 46, 108</p><p>Larger number = 108</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>LCM + HCF = 146 ....... (i)</p><p>LCM  -  HCF = 38 ....... (ii)</p><p>From (i) and (ii), we get -</p><p>LCM = 92</p><p>HCF = 54</p><p>Let, the numbers be x and (154  -  x).</p><p>x * (154  -  x) = 92 * 54</p><p>=> 154x  -  x<sup>2</sup> = 4968</p><p>=> x<sup>2</sup>  -  154x + 4968 = 0</p><p>=> x<sup>2</sup>  -  (46 + 108)x + 4968 = 0</p><p>=> x = 46, 108</p><p>Larger number = 108</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the difference of the mode and median of a date is 41, then the difference of the median and mean is?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2340;&#2367;&#2341;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2354;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 41 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["21", "20.5", "19", "19.5"], "options_hi": ["21", "20.5", "19", "19.5"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Given that,</p><p>Mode  -  Median = 41</p><p>Mode = 41 + Median</p><p>We know that,</p><p>Mode = 3 x Median  -  2 x Mean</p><p>41 + Median = 3 x Median  -  2 x Mean</p><p>41 = 2 x Median  -  2 x Mean</p><p>Median  -  Mean = 41/2 = 20.5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given that,</p><p>Mode  -  Median = 41</p><p>Mode = 41 + Median</p><p>We know that,</p><p>Mode = 3 x Median  -  2 x Mean</p><p>41 + Median = 3 x Median  -  2 x Mean</p><p>41 = 2 x Median  -  2 x Mean</p><p>Median  -  Mean = 41/2 = 20.5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}]}